<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Shaykh al-Mufid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 948–1022</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Shaykh al-Mufid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Shaykh al-Mufid was a Twelver Shia theologian and jurist of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and the leading Shia scholar of the Buyid period. He defended Shia doctrine in debates with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> and Mu'tazili opponents, adopting rational methods in theology, and his Kitab al-Irshad on the lives of the twelve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imams</a> remains a standard work. His students included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-sharif-al-murtada">al-Sharif al-Murtada</a> and al-Shaykh al-Tusi.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under their rule Twelver Shia scholarship flourished in Baghdad, with <b>al-Shaykh al-Mufid</b>, al-Sharif al-Murtada and al-Sharif al-Radi, compiler of the Nahj al-Balagha.</blockquote><a href="/empire/buyid-dynasty">Buyid dynasty · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=33.32,44.37&amp;year=996" aria-label="Baghdad on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5684 954 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of al-Shaykh al-Mufid"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6134 1224h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=33.32,44.37&amp;year=996">What was here in 996 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
